elster2mqtt (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Avoid busy-wait spinning during CAN receive timeouts.
  * Fix PUMPENSTATUS decoding for WPM 3 firmware.
  * Replace python-can with direct SocketCAN access.
  * Defer MQTT client import to client construction.
  * Resend read request once after a timeout.

 -- Juerg Haefliger <juergh@proton.me>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0200

elster2mqtt (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ignore unrelated ambient CAN bus frames during read
  * config: Remove byte swapping from PUMPENSTATUS
  * Add inter-query pacing in batch polling loop

 -- Juerg Haefliger <juergh@proton.me>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:03:22 +0200

elster2mqtt (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add cent_val formatter support for heating curve slopes.
  * Make CAN read timeout configurable via YAML and --timeout CLI flag.
  * Derive operational states and publish to dedicated status topic.
  * Decode actuator bitmasks and report active components.
  * Synthesize cumulative energy totals (kWh) and calculate JAZ and daily COP.
  * Update default configuration for Stiebel-Eltron WPM 3 and WPL 15 AS.
  * Add README with configuration reference, tuning guide, and Home Assistant setup.
  * Expand unit test suite covering state derivation, energy synthesis, and timeout.

 -- Juerg Haefliger <juergh@proton.me>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:15:00 +0200

elster2mqtt (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Match register ID in CAN read responses.
  * Handle CAN receive timeouts cleanly without crashing.
  * Allow decoding both 5- and 7-byte Elster frames.
  * Await MQTT message delivery and disconnect cleanly on exit.
  * Handle per-sensor timeouts gracefully in batch polling.
  * Correct response attributes on simulated reads.
  * Order systemd service after network-online.target.
  * Switch to debhelper-compat (= 13).
  * Expand package description in debian/control.
  * Standardize script entry point and package discovery.
  * Fix mock bus and expand test coverage.

 -- Juerg Haefliger <juergh@proton.me>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:05:00 +0200

